course: dictionary
lesson: 13414
title: Highlighter
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A highlighter is a pen with bright, see-through ink. You use it to mark the important words in a text, so they stand out when you come back to them. «Mia used a yellow highlighter to mark the key words in her science book.»
explain: Because the ink is see-through, you can still read the words under the colour. «Sam highlighted the answer to the question in pink, and he could still read every letter.»
explain: The clues in a sentence help you work out the meaning. Mia marks key words in her book, so a highlighter must be a pen used for marking. A good check is to swap in your meaning: "Mia used a yellow pen to mark the key words" still makes sense.
fact: A highlighter is a pen with bright, see-through ink.
fact: Pupils use highlighters to mark key words, facts and answers when they read.
fact: Highlighting helps with study and revision, because the important parts are easy to find later.
fact: «Highlighter» can also mean a make-up product that makes parts of the face look brighter.
fact: Phrases you may hear: yellow highlighter, highlighter pen, use a highlighter.
exercise: «Mia used a highlighter to mark the key words in her book.» What is a highlighter? | A book with a bright cover | *A pen with bright, see-through ink for marking words | A pencil for drawing pictures | A bag for carrying school books
exercise: Ellie wants to find the important facts quickly when she revises. What should she use? | *A highlighter | A rubber | A paper clip | A ruler
exercise: «Sam used a yellow highlighter to mark the answers.» Find and copy one word that names the pen. | *highlighter | yellow | answers | used
test: «The make-up artist brushed a highlighter on her cheeks so they shone.» In this sentence, highlighter means: | A pen for marking text | *A make-up product that makes the face look brighter | A small lamp | A book about art
test: Which sentence uses highlighter correctly? | Ravi put his highlighter in the sea | *Ravi used a highlighter to mark the key words | Ravi drew a highlighter on the wall | Ravi ate a highlighter for lunch
exam: Why do pupils use a highlighter when they read? | To draw pictures in the margin | To hide the words under the ink | To make the page smell nice | *To mark key words, facts and answers so they are easy to find
